      "page_title": "Exit Status: The Engine Behind Every Branch",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Zero Is True Here",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`0` = success/true; `1`-`255` = failure/false",
            "Inverted vs C, Python and most languages",
            "`$?` holds the last foreground command's status",
            "The very next command overwrites it — capture now"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "cmd",
            "rc=$?            # capture immediately",
            "true;  echo $?   # 0",
            "false; echo $?   # 1"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "run command",
              "status in `$?`",
              "`if` reads it",
              "branch taken"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "if Branches on a Command"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`if` tests no expression — it runs a command",
            "The branch is taken when that command exits `0`",
            "No `[` needed when a command answers the question",
            "`true` and `false` are real builtins returning 0 and 1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "if grep -q root /etc/passwd; then",
            "  echo 'root user present'",
            "fi",
            "if ! command -v git; then echo missing; fi"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Brackets Are Commands Too"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`test`, `[` and `[[` only produce an exit status",
            "`[` is a command; its last argument must be `]`",
            "`/usr/bin/[` exists — proof it is not syntax",
            "`[[` is the exception: a shell keyword"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Form",
            "Kind",
            "Where"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`test x = y`",
              "builtin",
              "POSIX"
            ],
            [
              "`[ x = y ]`",
              "builtin + binary",
              "POSIX"
            ],
            [
              "`[[ x = y ]]`",
              "keyword",
              "Bash only"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Chaining and Negation"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`&&` runs the right side only after status `0`",
            "`||` runs it only after a non-zero status",
            "`!` negates the status of a whole pipeline",
            "Pipeline status = LAST command; `set -o pipefail` = first failure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Not an if/else",
          "text": "`cmd1 && cmd2 || cmd3` — if `cmd2` fails, `cmd3` runs too. A classic silent bug; write a real `if`."
        },
